WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.634
-Right there,
that is five-time Grammy-winning

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:05.834
artist and producer
Robert Glasper in the house.

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:10.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:12.133
Thank you for being
here tonight.

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:17.567
With you is Derrick Hodge on
bass and Chris Dave on drums.

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:21.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:22.567
Robert, it's always great
to see you

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:24.400
and thank you for
for being here tonight.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.200
I appreciate this.
-Thanks for having me, man.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.400
-I just recently went to see --

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.133
Robert has a residency
at the Blue Note

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:34.334
here in New York City
in October.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.033
It's called Robtober.
-Robtober.

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:38.701
-Yeah. And it is unbelievable.

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:40.434
It's one of the best things
I've ever seen.

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:42.400
And every show
is completely different.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.300
-Completely different.
50 sold-out shows.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:49.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
-It was the best.

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:52.667
Like, do you know -- Like,
in a roundabout way,

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:56.234
you know, what you're going
to do set-list-wise or no?

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:58.367
-Not really. No.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:00.968
Because so many people come
and pop up on us

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:03.200
and, you know, it's always
kind of like jam session vibe,

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.534
so we kind of know.
But half of it we don't know,

00:01:05.534 --> 00:01:06.801
which makes it great, you know?

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:08.701
-Because you'll just start
playing something

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.634
and then all of a sudden you're
going into a different thing

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:12.267
and then you're playing
something, then like,

00:01:12.267 --> 00:01:13.701
can you just give a taste,
just noodle,

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:16.400
just play just something
just for fun?

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.167
[ Up-tempo jazz music plays ]

00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:34.200
♪♪

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:37.400
And then you throw in something.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.901
You start throwing in like
weird songs

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:43.167
on top of, like --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:44.467
You know what I think?
I don't know

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:45.901
if I got you in trouble
or whatever,

00:01:45.901 --> 00:01:47.767
because I went
and we had a great time

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:49.100
and I went back
to say what's up

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.968
and say hi to you and the band.

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:53.067
And then we went out --
In your dressing room,

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:54.901
out the window,
there's a giant piano.

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:57.000
-Yes.
-Outside the Blue Note.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.567
Like a scaffolding.
-Yeah.

00:01:58.567 --> 00:02:00.734
-And we kind of went
and stood on the scaffolding.

00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:03.267
-Ohh.
-No, safely.

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:05.067
-Yeah.
-No one knew.

00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:06.601
We didn't ask any permission.
We just did it.

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:09.634
-Yeah.
-Anyway, was it last night?

00:02:09.634 --> 00:02:13.834
-Sunday night,
the last night of the residency,

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:16.434
this dude, because he couldn't
get in because it was sold out.

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:19.000
So he scaled like Spider-Man.
He sailed --

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.734
He scaled the wall.
-Dude has got a video.

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:25.234
He scaled the wall
and then climbed on the piano

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:27.501
and got into his dressing room.
-Yeah.

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:28.968
Yeah, yeah, it was weird.

00:02:28.968 --> 00:02:30.400
-The city is crazy, man.
-That's commitment.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:31.701
-But that means I made it.

00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:33.834
-Yeah, yeah, you made it.
Exactly. You made it.

00:02:33.834 --> 00:02:37.667
That's exactly right.
I'm happy you're here.

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:39.767
Welcome. Chris,
what is that cymbal, by the way?

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:41.934
I've never seen anything
like that in my lifetime.

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:44.934
-It's called a spiral cymbal
as of now.

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:46.100
-Yeah.
-But the name changes.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:47.400
-I guess it's a great name
for it.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.033
-And my mom changes the name.

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:51.400
-It's like some kind of
really artsy Christmas tree.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:52.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.968 --> 00:02:56.100
But it's good.
But can you give me, like --

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.367
Alright, I'm going to close
my eyes, give me maybe a cymbal

00:02:58.367 --> 00:02:59.801
and then give me that cymbal
and I'll see

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:01.534
if I can decide
which one is which.

00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:02.934
♪♪

00:03:02.934 --> 00:03:04.434
That's not it.

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:05.467
That's it.

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:07.868
Oh.

00:03:08.334 --> 00:03:10.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:12.968
[ "Jeopardy!" theme plays ]

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:16.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:19.067
Alright. It's one of the two.
It's the second or third one.

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:22.300
But I think it's probably
that snaky sound.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.868
That second one
was like a rattlesnake.

00:03:24.934 --> 00:03:27.501
[ Cymbal playing ]
It wasn't it?

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:29.934
[ Cymbal plays ]
Oh, that was it.

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:32.801
What was the rattlesnake-y
sound?

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:34.267
That was that one?

00:03:34.267 --> 00:03:36.167
Alright. Alright.
We'll be playing around

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:37.501
with you guys all night.
I'm so happy you're here.

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:39.300
And thank you for being here.
Again, Robert Glasper.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:42.300
The best.

